WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.589 --> 00:00:31.539
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, this is going
to be a breakdown of the trailer and I’ve

00:00:31.539 --> 00:01:06.930
also got some news about the villains in X-Men
Apocalypse.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:20.520
Besides the obvious one.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:36.189
This is also going to be my bonus Marvel video
this week.

00:01:36.189 --> 00:02:11.630
If you’re just now finding me I do bonus
Marvel videos every Tuesday, be sure to subscribe

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:29.420
to get everything and leave me suggestion
for future bonus Marvel vids to do in the

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:30.420
future.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:38.140
In case you didn’t know, It’s coming May
23 in the US and May 22nd in the UK.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:41.819
So pretty much all of us will get to see it
at the same time.

00:02:41.819 --> 00:02:48.010
Let’s get going, I’m really just going
to focus on the new stuff in the trailer,

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:51.769
but since I haven’t done an X-Men video
since the first trailer, that’s a lot.

00:02:51.769 --> 00:02:54.299
So right off the bat they’re dropping the
Time Travel bomb.

00:02:54.299 --> 00:02:57.989
They’d implied this was happening in all
the trailers, Wolverine being sent back to

00:02:57.989 --> 00:03:03.720
rally Professor X and the X-Men against Bolivar
Trask.

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:07.790
The voice over explains why the Sentinels
are bad for everyone and we get a better look

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:08.790
at their ships.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:12.640
We saw that preview clip from the mtv movie
awards where they were dropping out of them

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:13.640
into battle.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:19.439
They remind me a lot of the way the Chitauri
living ships functioned in Avengers, just

00:03:19.439 --> 00:03:20.959
like troop ships.

00:03:20.959 --> 00:03:25.260
I’m really curious to see how they explain
both versions of Professor X talking to each

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:28.170
other psychically across time.

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:33.269
It’s an awesome visual, but it’s going
to have to jump through a few logic hoops

00:03:33.269 --> 00:03:46.459
based on mutant abilities in 
the future.

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:51.700
We see Wolverine going around and grabbing
Beast, who for some reason isn’t full on

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:54.939
Blue, unless he’s mystique in disguise.

00:03:54.939 --> 00:03:59.300
Bryan Singer is really good at making ensemble
films and thrillers, and I kind of think of

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:03.999
Days of Future Past as a Time Travel Political
Thriller with Mutants and Machines instead

00:04:03.999 --> 00:04:05.849
of James Bond.

00:04:05.849 --> 00:04:12.689
They show Magneto in prison and Mystique not
with him, so clearly something went wrong

00:04:12.689 --> 00:04:14.750
after the events of the last movie.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:18.500
I’m even more confused about the timeline
and Beast’s appearance now.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:24.620
We finally get the big Quicksilver Intro.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:28.490
The funny part is that they’re going to
use him to break his father, Magneto out of

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:31.500
the Pentagon prison.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:34.050
Love that Nixon poster in the background of
his home.

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:38.740
The breakout scene is also a little confusing,
I loved Xavier punching Magneto, but why can

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:41.150
he walk, when he was crippled during the last
movie.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:42.520
So many questions.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:46.449
They’re really laying it on thick here with
the Magneto Baseball stadium effect.

00:04:46.449 --> 00:04:49.889
They wanted to top that levitation scene from
the first movie.

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:53.920
I think this is kind of an absurd way to do
it, but I’ll wait till I see it in the context

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.130
of the story to judge.

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:58.940
Peter Dinklage is going to be epic as Boliver
Trask, just watch him on Game of Thrones if

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:00.340
you don’t believe me.

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:05.800
The design of the 70s sentinels is pretty
cool, but the future ones are really trippy.

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:08.300
I can’t wait to see the rest of what the
future looks like.

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:12.460
The ships and tech look amazing.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:17.000
We see bone claws Wolverine, like in the post
credits scene from The Wolverine movie last

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.000
year.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:22.919
In the promo images of future wolverine we
saw the adamantium claws, so I wonder if they

00:05:22.919 --> 00:05:28.020
just did that wrong, or if changing the past
gives future wolverine his normal claws back.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.740
More timeline questions.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:31.080
The final scene is also really awesome.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:35.539
I just love that Wolverine would tell someone
flat out what their future was.

00:05:35.539 --> 00:05:40.440
Most people would pause to consider the ramifications,
but Wolverine is just like Fuck Spoilers dude,

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.720
you totally die.

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:46.660
So the big news right now about X-Men Apocalypse,
the spiritual sequel to Days of Future Past

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:54.020
is that Mister Sinister will be in the movie
and Apocalypse of course.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:58.039
But Mister Sinister will be like the Loki
of the movie.

00:05:58.039 --> 00:06:05.150
As in the X-Men will be fighting him for most
of the movie before Apocalypse steps out of

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:06.150
the shadows.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:08.780
I think of him as being Fox’s version of
Thanos.

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:13.039
They’re the two biggest villains you could
possibly use, so neither studio wants to roll

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:14.039
them out too soon.

00:06:14.039 --> 00:06:17.000
That’s why it’s taken so many Marvel movies
to get to Thanos.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:21.550
There’s no word on what either Sinister
or Apocalypse will look like, but the story

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:26.230
will loosely be based on the Age of Apocalypse
storyline and supposedly they’re bringing

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:27.920
back Nightcrawler and Gambit.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:33.000
Here’s a quick breakdown of how you get
from Days of Future Past in the 70s to Age

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:35.090
of Apocalypse in the 80s.

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:39.530
In Days of Future Past the mutants are driven
to extinction, then attempt time travel as

00:06:39.530 --> 00:06:41.010
a way to change the future.

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:44.569
So even if they’re only a little successful
in changing what happens with the sentinels,

00:06:44.569 --> 00:06:46.229
they’ve created a whole new timeline.

00:06:46.229 --> 00:06:50.620
And the beauty of X-Men stories is that no
matter what you do, the outcome doesn’t

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:52.060
change too much.

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:56.849
So instead of being super happy hug time,
the new future created in Days of Future Past

00:06:56.849 --> 00:07:01.990
is still awful, it’s just overrun with minions
of Apocalypse, primarily Mister Sinister.

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:06.800
It’s like you swing from Humans dominating
Mutants to Evil Mutants dominating Humans

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:08.400
and Mutants.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.120
So it’s almost a worse future.

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:14.430
Since Bryan Singer said the plot would only
loosely be based on Age of Apocalypse, we’ll

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:20.360
have to wait for more information about the
cast to guess what they’ll change.

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:24.290
But Channing Tatum did confirm he was in talks
to play Gambit and if they’re bringing Nightcrawler

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:29.909
back they could shuffle the cast depending
on who dies during Days of Future Past.

